            <ArticleTitle>Acquisition of the mcr-1 gene by a high-risk clone of KPC-2-producing Klebsiella pneumoniae ST437/CC258, Brazil.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0732-8893(17)30309-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diagmicrobio.2017.09.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We identified one clinical isolate of K. pneumoniae harboring the mcr 1 (plasmid of IncX4 family) and blaKPC-2 (plasmid of IncFIB family) genes in southern Brazil. These findings highlight that K. pneumoniae isolates carrying both mcr-1 and blaKPC-2 may emergence as a serious threat to antimicrobial therapy.</AbstractText>
